# Production build settings. Vite reads this automatically for `npm run build`.
#
# Committed on purpose. Everything here is compiled into the JavaScript that ships to
# browsers, so none of it is secret — and keeping it in the repository means a production
# build is correct on any machine instead of depending on someone creating this file first.

# Deliberately EMPTY.
#
# Production serves the SPA and the API from one origin (the API proxied at /api), so an
# empty base makes every request relative: /api/... against whatever host served the page.
# No hostname is baked into the bundle, the same artifact works on any domain, and the
# worst deployment failure this app has — a live site quietly calling http://localhost:8000
# because the variable was never set — becomes impossible rather than merely unlikely.
#
# Set this ONLY if the API is ever moved to a different origin from the SPA, and then it
# must be the full scheme + host with no trailing slash (https://api.example.ca).
VITE_API_URL=
